Sun Sep 13 08:21:17 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 2.0.10:
  * Build switched from homegrown Makefile to Autotools, use the
    upstream dist tarball carrying generated configure and man page
  * Hook scripts returning failure codes now fail the run
  * VCSH_* variables are exported to hooks
  * vcsh status prints paths relative to $HOME
  * New flag to prefix vcsh foreach output with the repo name
  * write-ignore no longer requires a repo argument
  * Bash completion added, ZSH completion fixed
- Drop disable-tests.patch, the patched Makefile is gone upstream;
  pass --disable-tests to configure instead as perl(Shell::Command)
  is not in Factory
- ZSH completion moved to /usr/share/zsh/site-functions, matching
  upstream; ship new bash-completion subpackage
- Correct license to GPL-2.0-or-later per upstream SPDX tag

